                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A heavy-duty truck transmission is built to handle enormous loads, long miles, and demanding road conditions. But even the most durable systems can fail when wear, maintenance issues, or driving conditions take their toll.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For owner-operators and fleet managers, transmission problems can quickly turn into expensive downtime. When a truck isn't moving, neither is the business behind it. Understanding the common causes of heavy-duty truck transmission failure can help drivers catch problems early, protect their investment, and keep their trucks on the road longer.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-it-matters",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Transmission Health Matters for Heavy-Duty Trucks",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-it-matters"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A heavy-duty truck transmission plays one of the most critical roles in the entire drivetrain. It transfers engine power to the wheels while managing torque and shifting across a wide range of speeds and loads.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When it fails, the results can be serious:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-why-it-matters-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Costly repair bills"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Unexpected downtime"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Missed delivery schedules"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Reduced fuel efficiency"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Drivetrain issues are among the most expensive repairs for trucks and fleets. Preventive maintenance and early diagnosis are the best ways to avoid these problems.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-it-matters-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The best way to catch problems before they become costly issues is to schedule a service appointment with a reliable truck service provider. Schedule today with Sun State International to get a reliable expert opinion on your fleet's issues.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
