                },
                {
                  "id": "p-excessive-heat-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Heat is one of the biggest enemies of any transmission system. Heavy-duty trucks often operate in demanding environments, including:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-excessive-heat-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Long highway routes"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Stop-and-go city driving"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Hot climates"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Heavy cargo loads"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-excessive-heat-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When temperatures climb too high, transmission fluid begins to break down. Without proper lubrication, gears and bearings wear down faster.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-excessive-heat-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Signs of overheating transmission systems may include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
